  "question": {
    "text": "The most abundant elements by mass in the body of a healthy human adult are:<br /><br />Oxygen (61.4%); Carbon (22.9%), Hydrogen (10.0%); and Nitrogen (2.6%). The weight which a 75kg person would gain if all <math><msup><mrow><mi>&#160;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>H</mi></math> atoms are replaced by <math><msup><mrow><mi>&#160;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>H</mi></math> atoms is:"
